# inc-kgzx phase 2c: photograph the Undeath to Death Hit Dice pool SHORT, so
# fewest-Hit-Dice order (R1), the wasted remainder (R2) and the 9-HD cap (R3)
# are all visible in play.
#
# WHY THIS FILE CASTS TWICE. The pool walks creatures fewest Hit Dice first, so
# a 9-HD creature always sorts LAST, after every 1-HD and 8-HD one. The moment
# the pool cannot cover the next sub-cap creature the walk STOPS (R2), so a
# burst whose sub-cap creatures already exceed the pool can never reach the
# 9-HD creature, and a burst the pool can cover never wastes. The two rules are
# therefore mutually exclusive inside one walk: R2 and R3 cannot both be seen
# in a single cast, whatever the creature mix. This scene shows R1 + R2 in a
# first burst and R3 in a second, disjoint burst, which is the only way both
# are Observable rather than Reasoned.
#
# THE RULE, as lib/pspells.irh states it: aval AR_GLOBE, lval 4 (a 4-square
# burst centered on the aimed point, so the game's rounded-Chebyshev dist < 4),
# pval (LEVEL_MAX20)d4 -- ONE pool of 11d4 here, 11..44, per cast. Spent fewest
# Hit Dice first, ties nearest the centre; a creature of EF_HD_POOL_CAP (9) or
# more is skipped without spending; a remainder too small for the next creature
# is wasted and the walk stops.
#
# THE CASTER is an orc priest of Aiswin at character level 11 (Free
# Advancement), "Undeath to Death" learned through Learn Any Spell so it is
# innate and its caster level is ChallengeRating = 11. He stands in the Entry
# Chamber at (44,111), whose floor spans x=34..54, y=107..121. Wizard Sight
# (armed in the shared setup) makes the whole screen a defined target area;
# Freeze Monsters keeps every summoned undead on its square.
#
# BURST ONE -- R1 + R2, centre Cw = caster+4 east = (48,111):
#   claw A   caster+3,0  -> Cw-1,0  d1   1 HD   nearest the centre
#   claw B   caster+2,0  -> Cw-2,0  d2   1 HD   (R1: the farther claw second)
#   mummy 1  caster+4,0  -> Cw+0,0  d0   8 HD
#   mummy 2  caster+5,0  -> Cw+1,0  d1   8 HD
#   mummy 3  caster+6,0  -> Cw+2,0  d2   8 HD
#   mummy 4  caster+4,-1 -> Cw+0,-1 d1   8 HD
#   mummy 5  caster+4,+1 -> Cw+0,+1 d1   8 HD
#   mummy 6  caster+5,-1 -> Cw+1,-1 d1   8 HD
#   bodak    caster+4,-2 -> Cw+0,-2 d2   9 HD   AT the cap, near the centre
# The two claws and six mummies are 50 HD of eligible creatures, more than the
# maximum 11d4 = 44, so every seed wastes on a mummy and stops (R2). The bodak
# sits in the burst and is ACCEPTED by the undead filter (EF_LIM_MTYPE, tval
# MA_UNDEAD -- a bodak is MA_OUTSIDER carrying M_UNDEAD), so it never appears
# as REJECT-TARGET; being last it is never reached once the walk stops, which
# is why the cap itself is shown in burst two.
#
# BURST TWO -- R3, centre Cc = caster-6 east = (38,111), disjoint from burst
# one (their discs do not overlap; the caster is outside both):
#   claw     caster-7,0  -> Cc-1,0  d1   1 HD
#   bodak    caster-5,0  -> Cc+1,0  d1   9 HD   AT the cap, near the centre
# The pool covers the claw (1 HD) with 10..43 to spare and then reaches the
# bodak, which the cap skips without spending: SKIP-CAP, never REJECT-TARGET,
# never STRIKE. This is the line that proves the spell's undead filter accepts
# a bodak.
#
#   INCURSION_OPTIONS=tools/fixtures/options-2026-08-22.dat \
#   INCURSION_RUN_DIR="$PWD/logs/inc-kgzx/pool/seed-1" \
#   INCURSION_HDPOOL_PROBE=1 \
#       tools/headless.sh tools/keys/undeath-to-death-pool.keys 1
@include undeath-to-death-setup.keys

# =========================================================================
#  BURST ONE (centre Cw = caster+4 east): R1 order + R2 waste
# =========================================================================

# --- SUMMON claw A, caster+3 east (1 HD, nearest Cw) -----------------------
w
@choose "Monster Summoning"
TAB
@choose "Zombies"
@choose "crawling claw"
RIGHT*3
ENTER
@dump:summon-claw-a

# --- SUMMON claw B, caster+2 east (1 HD) -----------------------------------
w
@choose "Monster Summoning"
TAB
@choose "Zombies"
@choose "crawling claw"
RIGHT*2
ENTER
@dump:summon-claw-b

# --- SUMMON mummies 1..6 (8 HD, at mixed distances from Cw) -----------------
w
@choose "Monster Summoning"
@choose "Corporeal Undead"
@choose "mummy"
RIGHT*4
ENTER
@dump:summon-mummy-1

w
@choose "Monster Summoning"
@choose "Corporeal Undead"
@choose "mummy"
RIGHT*5
ENTER
@dump:summon-mummy-2

w
@choose "Monster Summoning"
@choose "Corporeal Undead"
@choose "mummy"
RIGHT*6
ENTER
@dump:summon-mummy-3

w
@choose "Monster Summoning"
@choose "Corporeal Undead"
@choose "mummy"
RIGHT*4
UP
ENTER
@dump:summon-mummy-4

w
@choose "Monster Summoning"
@choose "Corporeal Undead"
@choose "mummy"
RIGHT*4
DOWN
ENTER
@dump:summon-mummy-5

w
@choose "Monster Summoning"
@choose "Corporeal Undead"
@choose "mummy"
RIGHT*5
UP
ENTER
@dump:summon-mummy-6

# --- SUMMON the bodak near Cw, caster+4 east 2 north (9 HD, AT the cap) -----
w
@choose "Monster Summoning"
@choose "Outsiders"
@choose "bodak"
RIGHT*4
UP*2
ENTER
@dump:summon-bodak-w

# --- CAST ONE, centred on Cw (R1 order + R2 waste) -------------------------
# m opens the spell list; the shot opens in target mode (Q_TAR|Q_LOC, jump on)
# on the player. 'l' switches to the LOCATION cursor at the player, RIGHT*4
# moves it to Cw, ENTER confirms a bare location so the burst centres on Cw.
m
@choose "Undeath to Death"
l
RIGHT*4
@dump:target-prompt-1
ENTER
@while "more --" SPACE
@dump:after-cast-1

# =========================================================================
#  BURST TWO (centre Cc = caster-6 east): R3 cap, in a disjoint burst
# =========================================================================

# --- SUMMON claw, caster-7 east (1 HD) -------------------------------------
w
@choose "Monster Summoning"
TAB
@choose "Zombies"
@choose "crawling claw"
LEFT*7
ENTER
@dump:summon-claw-c

# --- SUMMON the bodak, caster-5 east (9 HD, AT the cap, near Cc) ------------
w
@choose "Monster Summoning"
@choose "Outsiders"
@choose "bodak"
LEFT*5
ENTER
@dump:summon-bodak-c

# --- CAST TWO, centred on Cc (R3: the bodak is SKIP-CAP) -------------------
m
@choose "Undeath to Death"
l
LEFT*6
@dump:target-prompt-2
ENTER
@while "more --" SPACE
@dump:after-cast-2
v
@dump:messages
@while "Messages" ESC
@quit
